From a543b930c1b581e9fc4f20bbf431708171a469a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:33:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] MetalSharp: MetalFX for the NGX bridge
 (IMTLD3D12CommandListExt) and MetalFX spatial upscaling at present
 (vkd3d.conf)

Command lists answer Mullion's IMTLD3D12CommandListExt (same IID and methods), so Mullion's nvngx.dll runs DLSS
Super Resolution and Ray Reconstruction on MetalFX's temporal and denoised scalers through MoltenVK (a scale chained
to a barrier, mvk_metalfx.h). vkd3d.conf (VKD3D_CONFIG_FILE, else ./vkd3d.conf; dxvk.conf's form) with
d3d12.metalSpatialUpscale (or d3d11's) = True keeps the swapchain at the back buffers' size and has MoltenVK upscale it
to the display with MetalFX's spatial scaler.
